"An Earth-born body holds no magic inside it at all."
"Magic-resistant alchemical ingredients permeate an Earth-born body's bones and brain."
"Those ingredients make an Earth-born newcomer difficult to affect with magic."
"This resistance is only a temporary quirk; it fades unless Davrar makes it a personal Talent."
"Davrar offers an Earth-born arrival a Talent to make the quirk permanent, in their first days."
"As a Talent, the resistance lets its holder resist and interfere with spells."
"The cost of that Talent is great difficulty ever casting magic of one's own."
"Magic items work less on the resistant Earth-born, and weak ones degrade in long contact."
"The resistance works less well on higher-tier spells."
"An Earth-born body feels loose magic as wisps, and structured spells as packed geometric wire."
"A resistant Earth-born can break a spell by finding its key element and subverting it."
"Magic resistance pushed hard under pressure is the root from which antimagic grows."
"Resistance ranks rise fast in a fight: Nathan's went from rank 4 to 10 in one fight."
"Translate yields only gibberish from Earth writing."
"An Earth-born mind may be taught a local language by a painful mental spell."
"Nathan was summoned by a spell tailored to a receptive mind with expertise in science."
"Other Earth-born arrivals were stolen to Davrar by Badud's lackeys."
"Earth is on the cusp of joining the Distal Expansion, the galactic civilization beyond Davrar."
"Later, with Immortal Body and Wizard's Palace, Nathan needs no brain to act."
"Later, Nathan regrows from a severed hand after being vaporized."
"Later, Nathan's body has been inviolate to mana almost since he arrived."
